    "notes": "Two exact creator CC0 natives confirm the historic buff-tiled corner department store: five main storeys, diagonal entrance bay with rounded porthole shoulders, stepped top and observation balcony, horizontal gridded glazing, concrete/iron balconies and open upper terrace. The rooftop image confirms the curved elevator-headhouse rail, damaged low wall and exposed stone torii/lantern precinct. Current whole/corner/balcony/porthole/terrace/shrine renders retain these identifying forms. Buff brick approximates fine grooved facade tile; hidden rear walls, exact roof arrangements, lettering, ceramic artwork and shrine positions remain medium-fi estimates. Temporary scaffolding, lights, merchandise and neighboring buildings are excluded."
